NOTE: This MIT license applies ONLY to the build scripts, the GitHub Actions
workflow, the fixture-generation script and the other original files in this
repository. It does NOT apply to the compiled ffprobe.exe or to any bundled
third-party component — FFmpeg, the MinGW-w64 runtime, libgcc, zlib — each of
which is governed by its own license. See the THIRD-PARTY-LICENSES/ directory
inside the release archive.

No patches are applied to the upstream FFmpeg sources; the build uses the
pinned upstream release tarball verbatim. Were a patch ever added here, it
would be a derivative work of LGPL-2.1 code and this MIT license would not
cover it — which is why CI fails on the presence of any *.patch or *.diff file.

The media fixtures in fixtures/ are synthetic, generated by tools/make-fixtures.sh
from FFmpeg's own testsrc2/sine generators and subtitle text written by that
script. They contain no third-party content and are covered by the MIT license
above.
